issues.failure_explanation:
The step $\gamma(\mathcal{M}^2\setminus A) \le ho_{max}
u_{max}\mathcal{L}^2(\mathcal{M}^2\setminus A)$ treats the coupling $\gamma$ as if it had a density bounded by $ho_{max}
u_{max}$ w.r.t. $\mathcal{L}^2$. No such bound holds for a general coupling of an atomic empirical measure with $
u$: e.g., with uniform densities ($ho_{max}=
u_{max}=1$), sets $B_1,B_2$ of measure $b$ and $A^c\supset B_1	imes B_2$ with $\mathcal{L}^2(A^c)=b^2$, the maximal coupling puts mass $\min(\mu(B_1),
u(B_2))=b$ on $A^c$, violating the claimed bound $ho_{max}
u_{max}\mathcal{L}^2(A^c)=b^2$ whenever $b<1$. Hence the lemma's conclusion fails for admissible couplings even when the stated event holds.
